# Cost & quota (adapted from laravel-phyzio)

## Reading / editing
- Grep first, then read only the lines needed. Do not re-read unchanged files.
- Smallest edit that solves the task; no refactors or "improvements" outside it.
- No new summary/report `.md` files in the repo; update the existing doc in 1–3 lines.
  (A diagnosis report the owner asks for goes in chat or an artifact, not the repo.)

## Tests
- Run only the test files for what changed, on `phyzioline_inventory_test`.
- Unrelated failure: check once with `git stash`, report in one line, do not fix it.
- New behaviour: 1 happy path + the main failure case.

## Process
- One task per chat. Unclear? ask ONE question before starting.
- Final reply: short, Egyptian Arabic — what's done / what's left / what I need from the owner.
- Stop when done; production deploys are manual — give the owner the commands.
